{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Before the cover of the ark, eastward; and before the cover of the ark he shall sprinkle of the blood with his finger seven times.</b> The sprinklings on Yom HaKippurim were eight: one above and seven below. And here I shall allude to you: one above corresponds to the supreme, first rank, which embraces within it חכמה and בינה, and seven below correspond to the seven. And we learned in tractate Yoma, chapter 'They brought him out' (הוציאו לו), and thus he would count: one; one and one; one and two; one and three; one and four; one and five; one and six; one and seven. And understand that when they said 'one,' it is the three (השלשה); and when they said 'one and one,' the meaning is the three (השלשה) and the great one (הגדולה); and so all of them to the end. And they said there in the Gemara: all agree at any rate that the first sprinkling requires counting with each and every one. What is the reason? Rabbi Eliezer says: so that he not err in the sprinkling. Rabbi Yochanan says: the verse says (ולפני הכפרת יזה שבע פעמים) — there is no need for the verse to say יזה; and what does יזה teach? It teaches about the first sprinkling, that it requires counting with each and every one. What is the difference between them? There is a difference between them in a case where he did not count and did not err — that is, he did not count the first sprinkling with all of them and did not err. The explanation of the matter is: according to Rabbi Eliezer he has fulfilled his obligation, since he did not err; and according to Rabbi Yochanan he has done nothing, even though he did not err, since he did not count the first with all of them. Contemplate what the intention of these Sages was in the reason for counting the sprinklings — and the sprinkling was in blood. <small>(In the Aggadah in the account of Nevuzaradan, and see Shemot Rabbah end of parashat Vayakhel.)</small> As for this blood that was upon it, they told him: from the blood of Yom HaKippurim that the High Priest sprinkled. Therefore it was placed upon the ark. And why is it called כפרת (cover)? Because it effects atonement (מכפרת) for the iniquities of Israel."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya writes השלשה ('the three') and הגדולה ('the great one') where standard printed editions of Yoma 55b read לפני ולפני ('before and before'); retained his reading hyper-literally as printed in the source text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:02.465476821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}